{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1496147-homebrew-brief-nightmares","id":1496147,"title":"[Homebrew] Brief Nightmares","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-02T19:14:24-07:00","id":1496147,"title":"[Homebrew] Brief Nightmares","content":"<u><b>The Voice In The Phone, Mister Close</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> &quot;Do you really think it's so unfair to do this to them, after all they did to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> His voice crawls with insistence and slithers with enthusiasm, and he keeps chuckling at something he thinks you should have figured out by now.<br /> <br /> Best At: 10 (Knowing What You Want, Bringing Out The Very Worst In You, Terrible And Subtle Murders)<br /> <br /> Worst At: 2 (Holding A Normal Conversation)<br /> <br /> Aspiration: Get Rid Of People You Hate<br /> <br /> Willpower/Scene: 6<br /> <br /> Initiative: 10<br /> <br /> Durability: 5<br /> <br /> Size: 1<br /> <br /> Structure: 6<br /> <br /> Dread Powers: Eye Spy, Immortal, Influence (Hatred 1), Know Soul, Miracle (Murder Only), Numen (Implant Mission, Sign)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Sleep Paralysis Angels, No Mouth &amp; No Eyes</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> &quot;We are just... ++TRYING++ to-to-to-to help <u>HELP</u> <i>help</i>, SoRRrrYYYy for [[whispering/screaming/sobbing X =&gt;<b>ETERNITY</b>&lt;=]]. Only way out is through-tears-dark-smile-dawn, hold our hands, follow (US!!! NOW!!! DANGER!!!)&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> They skip between places when unobserved and stick to the shadows, like they are afraid of something unspeakable happening to them for helping you, or maybe they are afraid of choosing the wrong person to help and thus disappointing someone important.<br /> <br /> Best At: 10 (Stalking And Observing, Identifying And Soothing Pain, Scaring Off Threats)<br /> <br /> Worst At: 2 (Approaching In A Non-Creepy Manner, Expressing Thoughts And Emotions)<br /> <br /> Aspiration: Help People Get Through Dangerous Times And Places<br /> <br /> Willpower/Scene: 6<br /> <br /> Initiative: 10<br /> <br /> Defense: 5<br /> <br /> Health: 12<br /> <br /> Speed: 10<br /> <br /> Dread Powers: Eye Spy, Immortal, Know Soul, Madness And Terror, Numen (Dreamshaping, Heal, Omen Trance)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Dinner &quot;Guest&quot;, Morsel-Of-Truth</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> &quot;I made myself all appetizing just for you, so you will show some appreciation if you know what's good for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Bloated, pale and aristocratic. He doesn't walk, he oozes and squelches. The dinner room becomes dark, save for his smile, and he insists that you don't ruin this ambiance.<br /> <br /> Best At: 10 (Kidnapping People, Extracting Secrets And Problems Via Mind Games, Tearing Apart Unwelcome Guests)<br /> <br /> Worst At: 2 (Noticing Peripheral Dangers Once The Dinner Begins, Fighting Without Sneaking Around)<br /> <br /> Aspiration: Force People To &quot;Enjoy&quot; Sharing &quot;Dinner&quot; With Him<br /> <br /> Willpower/Scene: 6<br /> <br /> Initiative: 10<br /> <br /> Defense: 5<br /> <br /> Health: N/A<br /> <br /> Speed: 10<br /> <br /> Dread Powers: Cannibalistic Communion (See Below), Chameleon, Immortal, Influence (Desperation 1), Maze, Natural Weapons 1 [Mouth-Hands], Surprise Entrance<br /> <br /> Ban: Can only enter someone's home if summoned, or if they have refused hospitality to a desperate person who requested it in earnest<br /> <br /> Bane: Bread dipped in consecrated salt and the blood of a human who overcame a compulsive eating disorder<br /> <br /> <b>Cannibalistic Communion:</b> When Morsel-Of-Truth has successfully kidnapped someone and prevented them from easily escaping, it can offer itself as a source of food and drink. The victim must consume such &quot;organs&quot; in a way that would inflict 1 Aggravated Damage on Morsel-Of-Truth per hour. During this, the entity coerces the victim into cutting its &quot;flesh&quot; and draining its &quot;blood&quot; in surgically precise ways. Furthermore, it demands that the victim demonstrate constant gratitude by revealing their secrets and problems, which the entity attempts with its Best Dice Pool, contested by the victim's Wits + Subterfuge. Each 1 Aggravated Damage worth of consumed &quot;flesh/blood&quot; places a Communion Token on the victim's sheet. Of note is that Morsel-Of-Truth lacks a Health Meter entirely, and therefore only runs out of &quot;flesh/blood&quot; when the victim escapes, when it is exposed to its Bane, or when the sun emerges on the horizon, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> These Communion Tokens can be used by the ST to inflict negative effects like Goblin Debt in Changeling 2ed Core. As compensation, the victim gains a number of Merit Dots equal to [Communion Tokens/2 Rounded Up] for the rest of the Story. These Merits must be traits that help the victim deal with the secrets and problems that they revealed to Morsel-Of-Truth. The victim can keep these Merit Dots after the end of the Story, but only if they willingly and knowingly summon Morsel-Of-Truth for another &quot;dinner&quot;, which requires the victim to set up a ritualistic space within their home which generates Open Condition [Desperation], leave an empty seat for Morsel-Of-Truth to manifest through, and say out loud &quot;the hole inside hurts, please make it stop&quot; 13 times around 1 AM.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Psychopomp Cat, Gunpowder</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> (Phantasmagorical echoes of bullet casings, rushing ambulances and mournful meowing.)<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Her collar has a spent bullet casing attached to it, along with her name. She gestures with her paw toward bullet holes and bloodstains on the wall, which form a message consisting of a name, address and date. You feel a cold hand on your shoulder and a hear a frightened whisper from behind you, but all you can see is the cat hissing and growling in the direction of the person that should have been there a moment ago.<br /> <br /> Best At: 10 (Delivering Messages And Finding Objects, Cooperating With And Calming Down Ghosts)<br /> <br /> Worst At: 2 (Obeying Instructions To The Letter, Resisting Offers Of Food And Games)<br /> <br /> Aspiration: Help Bring Closure To Unfinished Businesses<br /> <br /> Willpower/Scene: 6<br /> <br /> Initiative: 7<br /> <br /> Defense: 9<br /> <br /> Health: 5<br /> <br /> Speed: 13<br /> <br /> Dread Powers: Gatecrash (Underworld), Immortal, Know Soul, Numen (Occult Sight, Sign, Telepathy), Twilight Entity<br /> <br /> <b>Gatecrash:</b> A Horror with this Dread Power can open a gateway to other planes of existence (such as the Hedge, Primordial Dream, Shadow, Underworld or Astral Realms). The Horror spends a point of Willpower and makes an appropriate dice pool roll; if successful a gateway into the destination realm opens. The creature can hold the gate open for a number of turns equal to its Potency. Gatecrash can only open a gate to a specific realm, but may be selected multiple times, each time applying to specific Realm.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult Sight:</b> The entity is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. The entity notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of its senses and may make a Finesse + Resistance roll to approximate its distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Essence, it can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash of Wills using its Finesse + Rank as its die pool. Lastly, it may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Telepathy:</b> Entities with this Numen can reach out and link their minds with others, allowing instantaneous and reliable communication. This Numen costs one Essence. If the target chooses to resist, the roll is contested by the target\u2019s Resolve + Supernatural Advantage. Success allows the entity to freely communicate with the target and to read their thoughts until the end of the scene. If the target is mortal, they gain the Shaken Condition - being that intimate with an alien mind is profoundly disturbing.<br /> <br /> <b>Twilight Entity:</b> The creature exists in a Twilight state, at least in part. It can interact freely with entities in both the physical world and the twilight. For most creatures this interaction goes both ways, making it possible for ephemeral beings to attack them from Twilight. An intelligent creature might gain some control over how when it interacts with each world; the creature may spend a single point of Willpower to shift between its physical and immaterial states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-21-2023, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T15:01:47-08:00","id":1496546,"title":"","content":"Mind if I steal these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T15:58:46-08:00","id":1496552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1496147-homebrew-brief-nightmares?p=1496546#post1496546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind if I steal these?</div> </div> </div> </div>If by steal you mean use them in a Chronicle, sure. That's why I posted them. Just please mention that I wrote them. And if your Chronicle actually gets to a point where any of them shows up, please tell me how it turned out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T17:11:37-08:00","id":1496561,"title":"","content":"Yeah, should\u2019ve written that better. Obviously you will be credited. And yes, I\u2019ll happily fill you in on how everything goes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}